Why vendored rather than a submodule: the source is 124K, the repo must build
offline, and this project expects to fork it. Upstream's own README notes the
author maintains internal variants that also capture microphone input; if we
need timestamped dual-leg capture inside one process, that fork starts from this
tree. Pinning the commit here keeps that diff legible.

Upstream carries an explicit API-instability warning. Re-read its README before
bumping the pin.
